# Movies API (week 9 class 2) requests: sign up, log in, read with the token, log out.
# This is the conversation the web app (class2/00_warmup) has with the API: the same
# requests, with a person clicking instead of you. Run them TOP TO BOTTOM.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client), then "Send Request".
#
# Start the server first:
#   docker compose exec node node week09/class2/mflix-api/server.js

@api = http://localhost:3002/api

### 401 - reading needs a token now
GET {{api}}/movies?year=1999&limit=3

### 400 - every problem listed
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "NO SPACES", "password": "short" }

### 409 - taken (the demo users count)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "alice", "password": "correct-horse" }

### 201 - sign up. Send it twice to see the 409
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "dana", "password": "correct-horse" }

### 200 - log in; named, so the next requests can reuse its token
# @name dana
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "dana", "password": "correct-horse" }

### 200 - the same request as the first one, now with the token
GET {{api}}/movies?year=1999&limit=3
Authorization: Bearer {{dana.response.body.token}}

### 403 - dana is a viewer: signing up doesn't get you write access
POST {{api}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{dana.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Dana's Movie" }

### 204 - log out: the API revokes this token
POST {{api}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{dana.response.body.token}}

### 401 - same token, after logout
GET {{api}}/movies?year=1999&limit=3
Authorization: Bearer {{dana.response.body.token}}
